<item>
            <title>[LU-20679] Possible long processing of OBD_IDX_READ RPC</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20679</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The below is description of a real case:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;The LFSCK orphan scan on OST002b was initiated by MDT0002, however the vast majority of objects on that OST (~163M objects across 5,302 rbtree nodes) belong to sequence 0xe80000402 which is owned by MDT0001. As a result, lfsck_orphan_it_next() was performing expensive per-object disk lookups (ldiskfs directory search + LMA xattr + PFID xattr reads) for every single object, only to discard each one because it belongs to a different MDT. No objects were being added to the reply buffer, causing the OBD_IDX_READ RPC to spin for 40+ minutes without making any forward progress.
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It would make sense to change tgt_obd_idx_read() so that it respected the RPC deadline and return a partial reply (even if the buffer is empty) along with the last scanned position.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
